-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY ALGORITHMS IMPLEMENTED IN THIS WORK
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The DSP code here was written for this document and is not a copy of any
existing implementation. Several classes do, however, implement published
algorithms substantially as their authors formulated them. Mathematical
methods are not themselves subject to copyright, but the people who worked
them out are named here, and in full in the References section of the
document.

  Class `SVF` (state-variable filter)
      Implements the trapezoidal-integration formulation published by
      Andrew Simper (Cytomic), "Solving the Continuous SVF Equations Using
      Trapezoidal Integration and Equivalent Currents", November 2013.
      The g/k/a1/a2/a3 coefficients and the two-integrator update follow
      that paper.

  Function `polyBlep`
      Implements the PolyBLEP correction introduced in Vesa Valimaki and
      Antti Huovilainen, "Antialiasing Oscillators in Subtractive Synthesis",
      IEEE Signal Processing Magazine 24(2):116-125, March 2007.

  Class `Biquad`
      Uses the coefficient formulae from Robert Bristow-Johnson's
      "Audio EQ Cookbook", originally circulated as Audio-EQ-Cookbook.txt and
      adapted with permission as a W3C Working Group Note (2021).

  Class `Reverb`
      Implements the parallel-comb into series-allpass topology described in
      Manfred R. Schroeder, "Natural Sounding Artificial Reverberation",
      Journal of the Audio Engineering Society 10(3):219-223, July 1962, with
      the allpass structure from Schroeder and Logan (1961).

  Class `Ladder`
      Approximates the transistor ladder filter of Robert A. Moog,
      US Patent 3,475,623 (filed 1966, issued 1969; long expired), following
      the digital treatments of Stilson and Smith, and Huovilainen (DAFx-04).

  Function `Osc.white`
      A 32-bit xorshift generator per George Marsaglia, "Xorshift RNGs",
      Journal of Statistical Software 8(14):1-6, 2003.

